<p><em>Verification note:</em> Games dates, the Mizuho stadium, and the 18:00 window are taken from the Aichi-Nagoya organising documents and from guides that match them: the visitor PDF sets entry by 16:30 for the Sunday 4 October closing and shows 18:00 as the ceremony start; Wikipedia and a Nagoya guide describe the closing as 18:00 to 19:30 JST at the same stadium, also called Paloma Mizuho Stadium, with a handover to Doha for 2030. Sportstar’s schedule table also showed a 19:00 figure beside the closing. Treat 19:00 as unconfirmed against the visitor note. India’s medal count is a snapshot, not a closing tally. On 24 September, The Times of India and India.com reported India 15th with 17 medals: one gold, seven silver, nine bronze. That number will move before 4 October. ESPN, writing on 20 September, described a 501-member Indian contingent and Hangzhou 2023 as 106 medals, 28 gold, fourth place. This page does not publish a full closing medal table because the Games are still on.</p>
